    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>A self-governing British dominion formed on 31 May 1910 from the Cape, Natal, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/transvaal">Transvaal</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/orange-river">Orange River</a> colonies.</li><li>Its gold mines, migrant labour system and land laws built <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/africa">Africa</a>’s strongest economy on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/racial-segregation">racial segregation</a>.</li><li>It fought in both world wars, gained full <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sovereignty">sovereignty</a> in 1931 and became the apartheid republic in 1961.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>The Union had three capitals: <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pretoria">Pretoria</a> for the government, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cape-town">Cape Town</a> for parliament and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bloemfontein">Bloemfontein</a> for the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/appellate-division-of-the-supreme-court-of-south-africa">Appellate Division</a>, a compromise <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-africa">South Africa</a> still keeps.</p></aside>
    </section>

